<urn:atm:triage:finding/AV-HOTFIX-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AV-HOTFIX-001" ;
  triage:title "Host-qualified send is persisted into the local same-named mailbox and lost when the peer is unreachable" ;
  triage:description "Discovered during AV phase dogfooding: atm send fenix@rand-m5 -> daemon log 'handled send with outcome sent' with agent=fenix (local mailbox) BEFORE the peer dial; then peer_connection_pool 'direct peer TCP connect failed' and CLI error RemoteDeliveryUnconfirmed. Code: storage_and_nudge_router.rs commit_write persists first, dispatch_resolved_peer_write comment says 'record is already durable ... creates neither a second application route nor delivery recovery state' (ADR-057). Local ingress in message_handler.rs normalize_write does not strip the host, but the persisted record lands in the local (team, agent) mailbox, so the local fenix reads it as inbound and the remote never receives it, with no retry or outbox. Network context at observation time: rand-m5 was offline on Tailscale (last seen, rx 0) and mDNS gave only a link-local v6 address." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-av" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "arch-gate" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-05T18:20:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AV1B ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-05T18:10:43Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AV-HOTFIX-001/AV-001-persist> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AV-HOTFIX-001/AV-001-normalize> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "1" .

# DESIGN RULING (Rand, relayed via fenix, 2026-09-05T18:45Z; status remains
# "open", triage:dispatchReady stays false -- NO DISPATCH until fenix
# confirms bugs 2-4 rulings and the design is fully approved):
# Undeliverable host-qualified messages go into a durable outbound queue,
# tagged with a stale-by time/date per message. When the cross-host link is
# re-established, the queue is replayed IN ORDER; entries past their
# stale-by time are dropped/marked failed rather than replayed.
# Supporting facts fenix independently verified:
# - The receiver already dedupes replayed ULIDs via
#   DuplicateWriteDisposition::AlreadyDeliveredRemote in
#   crates/atm-core/src/send/delivery_persistence.rs -- so ADR-057's stated
#   premise of "no receiver idempotency" is stale and must be amended in the
#   same change that ships this fix.
# - The local-echo symptom traces to the mailbox key ignoring host: a
#   host-qualified write lands in the local same-named agent's own inbox
#   instead of being recognized as addressed to a remote peer.
# Rulings for the AV-HOTFIX-001 code paths beyond this design decision
# (bugs 2-4) are still pending and will follow one at a time.

# INTERIM-RULE ADDENDUM (Rand, relayed via fenix, 2026-09-05T18:45Z; still
# dispatch_ready=false): until the durable outbox design above is actually
# implemented, the interim behavior is an ERROR, not local persistence.
# Rand's own words: "if we do not have that design in place, there should
# be an error, not add it to the local mailbox and confuse agents with an
# errored self-send." Concretely: a host-qualified write must NOT be
# inserted into the local recipient's mailbox at all; if peer delivery
# fails, the CLI surfaces the error and nothing is left behind locally --
# no echo into the local same-named agent's inbox. This interim rule is
# the fix to dispatch now/first; the durable outbox is the follow-on
# design once approved.

